WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.660
In 1858, in a cave in south-west France,
a poor 14-year-old called Bernadette

2
00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:08.180
dug in the ground.

3
00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:09.660
A spring appeared.

4
00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:11.380
It still flows.

5
00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.730
Each evening, thousands
carry candles in procession,

6
00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.640
and the sick are given
the places at the front.

7
00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:21.960
Yet the Church has declared
only 72 cures miraculous.

8
00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.920
So if most sick pilgrims go home uncured,

9
00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:27.380
why do so many keep going?

10
00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:30.770
In this mission, you'll see
what pilgrims do at Lourdes:

11
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:34.600
the Grotto, the spring,
the candles and the baths.

12
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:39.350
Then you'll weigh up a hard question:
does a shrine bring anyone closer to God

13
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.240
than praying at home?

14
00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:46.110
Your mission: find out why so many
sick pilgrims keep going to Lourdes.
